    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0357" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg283"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 121.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 24, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 7th instant, No. 68,
                    together with its enclosure upon the subject of certain reports, to the effect
                    that a negotiation was in progress in Canada for the purpose of making peace
                    between the United States and the insurgents, has been received. The information
                    concerning the condition of the insurgent government, and the situation of their
                    affairs, which it is presumed will have reached you ere this, cannot but make
                    you aware of the falsity of the allegation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
